WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.944 --> 00:00:15.285
greeted the kids in the farmyard with a basket.

2
00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:18.888
"Please pick some spinach from the garden.

3
00:00:19.908 --> 00:00:22.070
We're making cheesy spinach balls today.

4
00:00:23.211 --> 00:00:25.372
Later you can feed my little helpers."

5
00:00:27.373 --> 00:00:28.434
Izzie was curious.

6
00:00:29.475 --> 00:00:33.284
"Do you mean the chickens and goats?"

7
00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:36.525
"No. You've never met these helpers," Chef said.

8
00:00:41.047 --> 00:00:43.048
The kids went to the garden and picked spinach.

9
00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:47.810
"I wonder who Chef's helpers are," Izzie said.

10
00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.931
"Maybe he got a pig!"

11
00:00:51.292 --> 00:00:52.012
Bobby said.

12
00:00:52.972 --> 00:00:53.693
Nina laughed.

13
00:00:54.213 --> 00:00:57.114
"Pigs aren't little!

14
00:00:57.894 --> 00:00:59.715
And they're not helpers, are they?"

15
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.761
In the kitchen Bobby read the recipe.

16
00:01:08.961 --> 00:01:11.662
"We have to cook the spinach in olive oil."

17
00:01:13.042 --> 00:01:16.083
Nina poured olive oil into a pan and turned on the burner.

18
00:01:17.263 --> 00:01:19.544
They dumped the spinach into the pan and stirred it.

19
00:01:21.184 --> 00:01:22.685
The leaves turned dark green.

20
00:01:24.405 --> 00:01:26.186
Chef removed the pan from the burner.

21
00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.546
"We'll let the spinach cool.

22
00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:31.987
Then we'll chop it and wring it out to dry it off."

23
00:01:33.088 --> 00:01:34.328
Chef handled the spinach.

24
00:01:35.964 --> 00:01:39.546
Izzie preheated the oven to 175 degrees Celsius.

25
00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:44.788
Nina grated Parmesan cheese, and Bobby chopped green onions.

26
00:01:46.468 --> 00:01:49.089
Izzie was still thinking about Chef's mystery helpers.

27
00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:52.031
"Chef, what do the helpers do?"

28
00:01:52.051 --> 00:01:55.012
"They keep my garden healthy."

29
00:01:55.032 --> 00:01:57.233
"Are they rabbits?"

30
00:01:57.693 --> 00:01:58.473
Nina asked.

31
00:01:59.674 --> 00:02:02.055
"Rabbits eat vegetables," Jason said.

32
00:02:02.075 --> 00:02:04.736
"Gardeners chase away rabbits."

33
00:02:06.536 --> 00:02:08.877
Izzie measured three-quarters cup of bread crumbs.

34
00:02:10.018 --> 00:02:11.358
She poured them into a bowl.

35
00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.580
Jason cracked an egg and beat it before adding it.

36
00:02:17.401 --> 00:02:19.481
Nina put in two tablespoons of yogurt.

37
00:02:20.742 --> 00:02:22.643
Chef added the chopped spinach.

38
00:02:22.663 --> 00:02:26.704
"Do your helpers like spinach balls?"

39
00:02:27.145 --> 00:02:27.845
Izzie asked.

40
00:02:28.605 --> 00:02:29.426
Chef smiled.

41
00:02:29.446 --> 00:02:31.506
"They love raw spinach."

42
00:02:33.347 --> 00:02:34.908
Chef melted butter in a pan.

43
00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.421
Then he poured it into the bowl.

44
00:02:41.122 --> 00:02:43.144
The kids added the cheese and green onion.

45
00:02:44.365 --> 00:02:47.467
Bobby sprinkled in half a teaspoon of paprika and pepper.

46
00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.550
Then they stirred all the ingredients together.

47
00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:57.093
"Form small balls with your hands," Chef said.

48
00:02:57.114 --> 00:03:00.036
"Squeeze them so they don't fall apart."

49
00:03:04.078 --> 00:03:06.180
The kids placed the balls on a baking sheet.

50
00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.861
Chef put them in the oven.

51
00:03:08.881 --> 00:03:13.323
"Now can we feed your helpers?"

52
00:03:13.763 --> 00:03:14.423
Izzie asked.

53
00:03:19.305 --> 00:03:21.006
Chef brought out a pail with a lid.

54
00:03:21.026 --> 00:03:22.747
"Here's their food."

55
00:03:23.907 --> 00:03:25.248
The kids peered inside.

56
00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:30.810
There were vegetable and fruit scraps, coffee grounds, and crushed eggshells.

57
00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:34.172
There were also torn pieces of cardboard.

58
00:03:35.776 --> 00:03:37.757
"It sure looks like pig food!"

59
00:03:38.037 --> 00:03:38.758
Bobby said.

60
00:03:40.279 --> 00:03:43.140
Ding! The spinach balls were finally ready.

61
00:03:46.942 --> 00:03:48.043
They each tried one.

62
00:03:48.063 --> 00:03:52.585
"Yum, cheesy and crunchy!"

63
00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:53.766
Nina said.

64
00:03:54.827 --> 00:03:55.867
Izzie looked at Chef.

65
00:03:55.887 --> 00:03:57.628
"Is it time?"

66
00:03:57.648 --> 00:04:03.912
"Yep." Chef led the kids out to the shed.

67
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:09.103
Inside was a bin with holes in the lid and the sides.

68
00:04:11.405 --> 00:04:12.346
He opened the lid.

69
00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:15.048
The bin was full of dirt.

70
00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.030
Chef turned on his phone's flashlight.

71
00:04:19.491 --> 00:04:20.933
Izzie saw something wiggly.

72
00:04:20.953 --> 00:04:26.217
"Earthworms! But how do they help you?"

73
00:04:26.237 --> 00:04:31.441
"After earthworms eat, they produce waste," Chef said.

74
00:04:31.461 --> 00:04:33.843
"Earthworm poop!"

75
00:04:34.223 --> 00:04:35.004
Jason said.

76
00:04:36.252 --> 00:04:37.713
"Yep," Chef said.

77
00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:40.554
"Their poop is full of nutrients.

78
00:04:41.694 --> 00:04:43.395
So I add it to the garden soil.

79
00:04:44.376 --> 00:04:47.697
It makes our plants really healthy."

80
00:04:47.717 --> 00:04:49.938
"Gross!" Bobby said.

81
00:04:50.798 --> 00:04:51.759
But Izzie grinned.

82
00:04:51.779 --> 00:04:53.900
"It's awesome!

83
00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.581
Can we feed the worms now?"

84
00:04:57.741 --> 00:04:58.482
Chef nodded.

85
00:05:01.323 --> 00:05:03.324
The kids emptied the scraps into the bin.

86
00:05:04.928 --> 00:05:07.194
"There you go, worms," Izzie said.

87
00:05:07.214 --> 00:05:10.583
"Thank you for keeping our garden healthy!"
